      "reason": "CESM2 and MPI-ESM1-2-LR provide native gn fields while GFDL-ESM4 is gr, which affects masks, exactness of operations and interpretation of differences on the same model's grid.",
      "status": "condensed",
      "notes": [
        "GFDL-ESM4 is `gr`: already remapped from 75 hybrid layers to 35 z levels (conserve_order1), an extra resolution difference; CESM2 (`gn`, 100 km) vs MPI (`gn`, 250 km) differ ~2.5×, so features narrower than the coarse grid are not comparable in amplitude."
      ]
    },
    {
